-> Common particle type definitions.
-> `LogException` is euglena's own logging particle — deliberately not
-> named `Exception`, since that name is now the language's built-in
-> exception type (T30) and has a different shape (message/innerException).
Log = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "Log", message ∈ String, level ∈ String }
LogException = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "LogException", source ∈ String, message ∈ String }
ACK = Particle ∩ { _class ∈ "ACK", source ∈ String }
